build: 2026-06-22 v10.38.0 (Audio Clips + MIDI import + Unison)
branch: claude/piano-roll-clip-view-wozlie
includes: AUDIO CLIPS (new): Tools ▸ Audio & Bio ▸ Audio Clip — import any audio file (WAV · AIFF · MP3 · M4A · …) and play it as a CLIP: trim Start/End, Loop, set its Gain, with Play/Stop. The clip plays through a self-contained player attached additively to the master mix (no master-output surgery) — the foundation the timeline/ClipStore builds on next. MIDI IMPORT (new): Tools ▸ Editors ▸ Import MIDI — bring a Standard MIDI File (Type 0/1) onto the piano roll. Melodic notes are parsed (GM drums on channel 10 excluded), then folded onto the single visible bar: first-bar notes, length clamped to the bar, pitch octave-folded into the visible range — so a DAW clip lands comprehensibly on Echoel's grid. Completes the SMF round-trip (export already shipped). UNISON (new): a played note can stack up to 3 detuned voices, symmetrically spread in cents and panned across the stereo field (1/√n gain so loudness stays sane) for a thick, ensemble sound. It's a per-sound control in Tools ▸ Editors ▸ Sound (Unison ▸ Voices · Detune) and saves with the patch; Bright Lead (2 voices / 10 cents) and Vapor Lead (3 / 12) ship a gentle default, while pads/keys stay clean for full polyphony. Off is bit-identical to before; the audio-thread note path was reviewed (no allocation/locks/ObjC/GCD/IO) and the engine is unit-tested (allocation/clamp/release/finite-render). Patches saved before unison still load (decode-safe). Builds on v10.37.1 (per-channel insert FX on both drum paths + Channel Rack). All Xcode-Compile-Check green per commit. Still honestly held for a dedicated cycle: automation playback wiring + multi-track arrangement timeline (parallel lanes) + video capture/edit.
